        "text": "Ursula Walowski was elected to the circuit court in 2008 after working as a state prosecutor for 15 years. She serves in the Criminal Division. During her recent term, the Illinois Appellate Court overturned her rulings at least 25 times, the highest number among criminal judges on the 2026 retention ballot. Two defendants have been charged with attacking public defenders in her courtroom since 2025.",
